    "key": "description",
    "content": "Revered American writer and wit, born Samuel Clemens (1835) in Florida, Missouri; author of Tom Sawyer (1876) and Huckleberry Finn (1884), and one of the first Americans, in 1866, to offer a published account of surfing—or \"surf-bathing\" as Twain called it. Twain, 30, was virtually unknown when he visited the Kona Coast on the Big Island of Hawaii as a $20-dollar-an-article travel correspondent fo..."
